{"content": "### Configure uv as the build backend in pyproject.toml

Source: https://github.com/astral-sh/uv/blob/main/docs/concepts/build-backend.md

Add uv_build to the [build-system] section to build pure Python wheels and source distributions. Including an upper version bound prevents unexpected breaking changes.

```toml
[build-system]
requires = ["uv_build>=0.12.9,<0.13"]
build-backend = "uv_build"
```

--------------------------------

### Configure path dependencies in pyproject.toml

Source: https://github.com/astral-sh/uv/blob/main/docs/concepts/projects/workspaces.md

Use path dependencies under `tool.uv.sources` when members require distinct virtual environments or have conflicting dependency constraints. Note that `uv run --package` is unavailable in this standalone mode.

```toml
[project]
name = "albatross"
version = "0.1.0"
requires-python = ">=3.12"
dependencies = ["bird-feeder", "tqdm>=4,<5"]

[tool.uv.sources]
bird-feeder = { path = "packages/bird-feeder" }

[build-system]
requires = ["uv_build>=0.12.9,<0.13"]
build-backend = "uv_build"
```

--------------------------------

### Add development dependency using uv CLI

Source: https://github.com/astral-sh/uv/blob/main/docs/concepts/projects/dependencies.md

Adds a dependency to the default dev dependency group. Development dependencies are local-only and not packaged for distribution.

```console
$ uv add --dev pytest
```

--------------------------------

### BuildBackendSettings struct with all four configuration fields

Source: https://github.com/astral-sh/uv/blob/main/crates/uv-build-backend/src/settings.rs

The `BuildBackendSettings` struct defines all four requested configuration options under `[tool.uv.build-backend]`. The `#[serde(rename_all = "kebab-case")]` attribute maps TOML keys like `module-root` to the Rust field `module_root`.

- **`module-root`** (default `"src"`): Directory containing the module directory.
- **`module-name`** (default `None`): Name of the module directory; inferred from package name if unset. Accepts a single string or a list of strings for namespace packages.
- **`source-exclude`** (default `[]`): Globs for files/directories to exclude from the source distribution (also applied to wheels for consistency).
- **`wheel-exclude`** (default `[]`): Globs for files/directories to exclude only from the wheel.

```rust
/// Settings for the uv build backend (`uv_build`).
///
/// Note that those settings only apply when using the `uv_build` backend, other build backends
/// (such as hatchling) have their own configuration.
///
/// All options that accept globs use the portable glob patterns from
/// [PEP 639](https://packaging.python.org/en/latest/specifications/glob-patterns/).
#[derive(Deserialize, Serialize, OptionsMetadata, Debug, Clone, PartialEq, Eq)]
#[serde(default, rename_all = "kebab-case")]
#[cfg_attr(feature = "schemars", derive(schemars::JsonSchema))]
pub struct BuildBackendSettings {
    /// The directory that contains the module directory.
    ///
    /// Common values are `src` (src layout, the default) or an empty path (flat layout).
    #[option(
        default = r#""src""#,
        value_type = "str",
        example = r#"module-root = """#
    )]
    pub(crate) module_root: PathBuf,

    /// The name of the module directory inside `module-root`.
    ///
    /// The default module name is the package name with dots and dashes replaced by underscores.
    #[option(
        default = r#"None"#,
        value_type = "str | list[str]",
        example = r#"module-name = "sklearn""#
    )]
    pub(crate) module_name: Option<ModuleName>,

    /// Glob expressions which files and directories to exclude from the source distribution.
    ///
    /// These exclusions are also applied to wheels to ensure that a wheel built from a source tree
    /// is consistent with a wheel built from a source distribution.
    #[option(
        default = r#"[]"#,
        value_type = "list[str]",
        example = r#"source-exclude = ["*.bin"]"#
    )]
    pub(crate) source_exclude: Vec<String>,

    /// Glob expressions which files and directories to exclude from the wheel.
    #[option(
        default = r#"[]"#,
        value_type = "list[str]",
        example = r#"wheel-exclude = ["*.bin"]"#
    )]
    pub(crate) wheel_exclude: Vec<String>,
}
```

--------------------------------

### Default cache keys when tool.uv.cache-keys is not specified

Source: https://github.com/astral-sh/uv/blob/main/crates/uv-cache-info/src/cache_info.rs

When no cache-keys are configured, uv defaults to watching pyproject.toml, setup.py, setup.cfg, and the src directory for modification time changes to determine whether to rebuild.

```rust
        // If no cache keys were defined, use the defaults.
        let cache_keys = cache_keys.unwrap_or_else(|| {
            vec![
                CacheKey::Path(Cow::Borrowed("pyproject.toml")),
                CacheKey::Path(Cow::Borrowed("setup.py")),
                CacheKey::Path(Cow::Borrowed("setup.cfg")),
                CacheKey::Directory {
                    dir: Cow::Borrowed("src"),
                },
            ]
        });
```", "results": []}
